course: dictionary
lesson: 12588
title: Showing disapproval
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disapproval means the feeling that something is bad, wrong or not acceptable. When you feel it, you think the thing should not have happened. «Dad gave me a look of disapproval when we tracked mud across the kitchen.» The look shows his feeling without any words.
explain: People can show disapproval without speaking: with a frown, a «tut» or a shake of the head. «The teacher shook her head in disapproval.» Use the clues to check: a head shake is not a smile or a cheer, so it must mean no.
explain: Look for the phrases that often go with this word: «a look of disapproval», «shake your head in disapproval» and «to show disapproval of» something. If you can swap in the word «unhappy with» and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Disapproval is a noun. It names a feeling.
fact: «Disapproval» means the feeling that something is bad, wrong or not acceptable.
fact: You can show disapproval by a look, a word or a sound, such as a «tut».
fact: Phrases to learn: «a look of disapproval», «shake your head in disapproval», «to show disapproval of» rude behaviour.
exercise: «Mum gave me a look of disapproval when I ate the last biscuit.» What does disapproval mean here? | Feeling hungry for more | *Feeling that what you did was wrong | Feeling sleepy after a big meal | Feeling pleased about something
exercise: «The teacher shook her head in disapproval.» Which action shows disapproval? | Clapping her hands | Smiling broadly | *Shaking her head | Opening the window wide
exercise: Which of these shows disapproval? | Clapping at the end of a song | A big hug for a friend | *A tut and a frown | A loud cheer and a big smile
test: Which sound from a parent often shows disapproval? | A giggle | *A tut | A yawn
test: Which word means the feeling that something is wrong or not acceptable? | Surprise | Boredom | *Disapproval
exam: What does disapproval mean? | Being very tired after a long day | *The feeling that something is bad, wrong or not acceptable | Running away quickly from danger | Being very happy about something
